The project aims to implement a python CLI to detect deadcode in a codebase with multiple languages supported.

In the /specs folder you will find for each folders the programming language to support.

Inside each language folder you will find two types of files:

1/ *.collector files

It contains the specs for the collector to implement.
THe description of the collector to implement.
Then there is multiples example of files that will be used to test the collector.
And finally the expected output of the collector in JSON.

2/ *.rule files

It contains the rules to detect deadcode. 
There is first a description of what the rule is about. 
Then it describes which collector is needed to as an input to the rule.
Then there is multiples example of files that will be used to test the rule.
And finally the expected output of the rule in JSON.


The CLI command is executed with the following command: `deadcode <path> -<language/folder name in specs/> -r 01_unused_function.rule`. 

By default the command will return the JSON output as stated in the *.rule file. 



